{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Elem","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Elem","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Image"],"declarations":50,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_ofTerms_pair_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_ofTerms_pair_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":500,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L500-L525","doc":"**A two-term relation in context is the same two terms, in context.**\n\nEvery rule in a two-term presentation — braid, far-commutation, Bokut–Shiao —\nhas this shape, and an S-polynomial is built out of exactly two such\ncontext-multiplications. Computing one from the `excise` definition each time is\nthe same case split every time; this does it once.\n\nThe proof is the only place the shape condition has to be reasoned about: on the\nshape `a ++ w ++ b` both sides reduce to append-cancellation, and off it both\nsides are zero because a matching term would exhibit the missing `w`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_ofTerms_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_ofTerms_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":465,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L465-L498","doc":"**A relation in context is the same terms, in context.**\n\n`contextMul` is defined through `excise`, so reading a coefficient off it is a\ncase split on whether the monomial has the shape `a ++ _ ++ b`. That split is the\nsame every time; this does it once, for a relation given by an explicit term\nlist. Every rule in a finite presentation is such a list, and every S-polynomial\nis two context-multiplications of them, so this is the lemma that keeps a\ncomposition's proof to word identities plus `split_ifs`.\n\nThe shape case split is the outer `by_cases`; the induction on `L` inside it only\nhas to push `List.filter` through `List.map`, because `w ↦ a ++ w ++ b` is\ninjective and append-cancellation is `simp`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_coeff_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_coeff_congr","kind":"theorem","line":452,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L452-L463","doc":"`contextMul` sees only the coefficient function, so it respects `CoeffEq`.\n\nNeeded because `ofTerms` is a *representation*: the same element written with its\nterms in a different order is a different value of `AlgElement` (different\n`support`, different `coeff` term), so a rule can only be matched against a\nnormal form up to coefficients. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.ofTerms_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.ofTerms_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":447,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L447-L450","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.ofTerms_support_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.ofTerms_support_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L435-L445","doc":"`ofTerms` with a nonempty term list has nonempty support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.ofTerms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.ofTerms","kind":"def","line":416,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L416-L433","doc":"Build an algebra element from a list of (monomial, coefficient) pairs.\nThis is the primary constructor for rewriting rule relations. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.leftMulWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.leftMulWord","kind":"def","line":407,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L407-L412","doc":"Left-multiply by a word (list of generators): `w · f`.\nDefined by folding `leftMulGen` from right to left:\n`[g₁, g₂, g₃] · f = g₁ · (g₂ · (g₃ · f))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.rightMulGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.rightMulGen","kind":"def","line":381,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L381-L405","doc":"Right-multiply by a single generator: `f · g`.\nAppends `g` to every monomial in the support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.leftMulGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.leftMulGen","kind":"def","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L354-L379","doc":"Left-multiply by a single generator: `g · f`.\nPrepends `g` to every monomial in the support.\n\n`(g · f).coeff (g :: t) = f.coeff t` and `(g · f).coeff other = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_nil_nil_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_nil_nil_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L347-L350","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_gen_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_gen_comm","kind":"theorem","line":320,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L320-L345","doc":"**Sliding a single generator across an element that commutes with it.**\n\nIf every monomial of `f` commutes with `x` *as a word* — `w ++ [x] = [x] ++ w` —\nthen multiplying on the right by `x` and multiplying on the left by `x` give the\nsame element.\n\nThis is the shape of a rule composed with itself over `xxx` when its relation is\na polynomial in the one generator `x`: the two halves of the S-polynomial are\nthis element slid past the same letter, so the S-polynomial vanishes outright\nrather than merely reducing to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_coeff_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_coeff_neg","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L306-L318","doc":"`contextMul` sends a coefficientwise negation to a coefficientwise negation.\n\nThe transfer lemma of §6 runs on this: a rule and its negative give\nS-polynomials that are negatives of each other, and the two halves of an\nS-polynomial are context-multiplications. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_shape","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L293-L304","doc":"Every monomial carrying a non-zero coefficient in `a · f · b` has the\nshape `a ++ w ++ b` with `w` carrying a non-zero coefficient in `f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_coeff_of_not_shape","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_coeff_of_not_shape","kind":"theorem","line":286,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L286-L291","doc":"Off the shape `a ++ _ ++ b` the coefficient is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_coeff_middle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul_coeff_middle","kind":"theorem","line":280,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L280-L284","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.contextMul","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L260-L278","doc":"**Context multiplication** `a · f · b`: multiply `f` on the left by the\nmonomial `a` and on the right by the monomial `b`.\n\nThis is the operation a rewriting step is built from — replacing an\noccurrence of a rule's leading monomial *inside* a larger word means\nsubtracting `c • (a · relation · b)`. It is exact (no convolution needed)\nbecause `a` and `b` are monomials: the coefficient of `a ++ w ++ b` is the\ncoefficient of `w`, and every other monomial gets `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.sub_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.sub_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L255-L256","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.sub","kind":"def","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L252-L253","doc":"Subtract: `f - g`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.neg_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.neg_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L249-L250","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.neg","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L241-L247","doc":"Negate an algebra element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.smul_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.smul_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L238-L239","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.smul","kind":"def","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L230-L236","doc":"Scalar multiply: `c • f`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.add_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.add_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L227-L228","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.add","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L217-L225","doc":"Add two algebra elements.  Support is the union (possibly\nan oversized superset due to cancellation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.eraseCoeff_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.eraseCoeff_support","kind":"theorem","line":212,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L212-L213","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.eraseCoeff_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.eraseCoeff_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":207,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L207-L210","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.eraseCoeff_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.eraseCoeff_self","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L202-L205","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.eraseCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.eraseCoeff","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L190-L200","doc":"Zero out the coefficient at one monomial.  Used to peel an element apart\none term at a time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.singleton_coeff_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.singleton_coeff_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L185-L188","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.singleton_coeff_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.singleton_coeff_self","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L181-L183","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.singleton_support_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.singleton_support_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L174-L179","doc":"The singleton of a monomial has nonempty support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.singleton","kind":"def","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L169-L172","doc":"A single monomial with coefficient 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.single_coeff_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.single_coeff_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L163-L167","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.single_coeff_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.single_coeff_self","kind":"theorem","line":158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L158-L161","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.single","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.single","kind":"def","line":141,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L141-L156","doc":"A single monomial with coefficient `c`.  The basis of all\n`AlgElement` construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.mem_support_of_coeff_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.mem_support_of_coeff_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L133-L137","doc":"A monomial carrying a non-zero coefficient lies in the support. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.isZero_of_support_eq_empty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.isZero_of_support_eq_empty","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L129-L131","doc":"A representation with empty support is zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.isZero_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.isZero_zero","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L127-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.isZero","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L116-L125","doc":"An element **is zero** when every coefficient vanishes.\n\nNote this is *not* `f.support = ∅`: the support field is an arbitrary\nsuperset of `{m | coeff m ≠ 0}`, so `support = ∅` is a statement about the\nchosen representation and not about the element. (It was the earlier\ndefinition; with a representation-independent notion of reduction it would\nmake `IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` unsatisfiable rather than merely wrong,\nsince the difference `f - f` carries the support `f.support ∪ f.support`.)\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.CoeffEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.CoeffEq","kind":"def","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L110-L114","doc":"**Equality of elements.** `AlgElement` is a representation, not a\nquotient: the `support` field is a superset of the true support, so two\nstructurally different values can denote the same element of `k⟨G⟩`.\n`CoeffEq` is the equality that means anything mathematically. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.zero","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L104-L108","doc":"The zero element of the free algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.support_spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.support_spec","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Coefficients outside the support are zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.support","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L96-L96","doc":"The support is finite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.coeff","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L94-L94","doc":"Coefficient of each monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement.mk","kind":"ctor","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L92-L92","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AlgElement","kind":"structure","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L87-L98","doc":"An element of the free associative algebra `k⟨G⟩` over a ring `k`,\nrepresented as a finitely-supported linear combination of monomials.\n\nFor the formalization we work abstractly: an element is a function\nfrom monomials to coefficients with finite support. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:monomial-basis","label":"def:monomial-basis","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/monomial-basis.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.excise_eq_of_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.excise_eq_of_eq","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L79-L83","doc":"The middle factor is uniquely determined: if `m = a ++ w ++ b` then\n`w = excise a m b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.excise_middle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.excise_middle","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L73-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.excise","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.excise","kind":"def","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L65-L71","doc":"`excise a m b` is the candidate middle factor of `m` between the contexts\n`a` and `b`: drop `|a|` letters from the front and `|b|` from the back.\nIt is the *only* possible `w` with `m = a ++ w ++ b`, which is what makes\nthe shape test in `contextMul` a decidable equation rather than an\nexistential. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Monomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Monomial","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Elem.lean#L60-L63","doc":"A **monomial** in a free associative algebra on generators of type `G`.\nRepresented as a list (word) of generators, with `[]` as the empty\nmonomial (unit `1`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}